  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/misc5/). VERDICT: CURRENT. 2026-11-01 review @100b6fbb6e: is_test_path and is_test_file both return False for packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/recorded/aardvark_dns/crate/src/main.rs. `hypergumbo --backend tree-sitter survey packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer` reports rust files=16 test_files=2; the 14 non-test files are all under recorded/. Repo-wide count is unchanged (git ls-files '*.rs' = 19, the other 5 are test fixtures or src/test). WI-dibuf (d3bbf8bdcf) unified the predicates but added no recorded/ rule. Premise holds as filed. MECHANISM: shared test-path predicates (is_test_path/is_test_file) have no rule for a recorded-fixture directory (recorded/). SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-ritaf(done)."  # 707b
- op: discuss  # 4b05
  at: '2026-11-13T09:23:20Z'  # 4b05
  by: agent  # 4b05
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4b05
  clock: 3  # 4b05
  nonce: 4b05  # 4b05
  message: "2026-11-13, from an outside reader's review of a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run (batch tag outside_reader_review_20261113; re-checked on dev d6a8a140e7). The missing test-support classification has three more consequences than the profile count in the title. (1) Entry points: the recorded crate's Rust main() and the main of recorded/sample_project/pkg/app.py are listed under Entry Points at every sketch budget; entrypoints.py demotes test code by is_test_node, which these paths do not match. (2) Tiered survey: 25 of the 143 nodes in survey.64k.json are under recorded/, and that file opens with the crate's edges. (3) The sketch Tests line lists cargo test for a repo whose own tests are all pytest. Key Symbols also gives the crate 4 file headings at 32k and 6 at 128k. GENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13): the fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language, and a rule naming the directory recorded/ does not close this item. Candidates to weigh: a tree that only test code reads or references is test input; a tree holding its own project manifest that no build of the enclosing project includes is not first-party source; a user-declared key in .hypergumbo.toml for trees the two rules miss. Other repos keep such trees under testdata/, fixtures/, golden/, snapshots/, cassettes/, corpus/, samples/ and under names of their own, in every language. Acceptance should include at least two repositories that are not hypergumbo, in two languages, each with a recorded or fixture project that holds an entry point."  # 4b05
