  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-15: this item goes in PR 3 of the plan at ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/PLAN.md (after the stable-id bump PR, before the release), as the first commit among the entry-point items, ahead of WI-mapaj-mirig-guhon-mavav-bujis-madaj-tuguh-fivuz. Not in the bump PR: its rule is not designed yet, and the bump PR has to stay attributable to id changes. Still to do, unchanged: a rule that names no directory (owner, 11-13), a measurement of what else it reclassifies, acceptance on two outside repositories in two languages. Measured on dev 4eb555b680: every test file imports paths.py and selection/filters.py, so an import-time change there selects the whole suite in CI."  # 937e
- op: discuss  # 08f2
  at: '2026-11-16T19:01:10Z'  # 08f2
  by: agent  # 08f2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 08f2
  clock: 6  # 08f2
  nonce: 08f2  # 08f2
  message: "NOT IN PR #2203. OWNER RULING 2026-11-16: PR 3 shipped without this item; the fix is a `.hypergumbo.toml` key that declares test-input trees, built AFTER the release, alongside WI-buzup. No status change. WHY: a census of 661 embedded project trees in 44 repositories, 292 judged test input (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr3/fosuk_census.md, table fosuk_census.tsv; I recomputed the scores from the table), found that no rule computed from repository content separates fixture trees from first-party code. Found / wrongly demoted: 'only test code references the tree' 6 / 4; 'own manifest that no build includes' 37 / 106 (it would demote 1,309 entry points, including all eight of hypergumbo's own packages); 'a test file has a graph edge into the tree' 0 / 2; a reference-and-graph rule devised during the census 22 / 1 (the only one that classifies both recorded trees here; designed on the same rows, generalisation not shown; needs the linked graph). 13 fixtures are missed by every rule. WHAT THE KEY HAS TO SOLVE (census Part A): the predicates are pure path functions with 63 consumer calls, 24 of which have no repository root in scope (the entry-point demotion at entrypoints.py among them); saved maps persist `profile` but not the file list, so commands that re-read a map need the declared roots persisted; test classification takes code out of taint-source scope in verify-claims, so a repository-supplied declaration needs a visible reason string. `.hypergumbo.toml` exists (user_config.py; unknown keys raise) and hypergumbo's own tree has none. ACCEPTANCE AS RULED 11-13 still applies: no directory named in code; two outside repositories in two languages (the census names candidates: fx internal/e2e [Go], eclipse.jdt.ls projects [Java], automerge packaging_tests [JavaScript], haskell-language-server ghcide-test/data [Haskell])."  # 08f2
- op: discuss  # d43f
  at: '2026-11-16T23:29:21Z'  # d43f
  by: agent  # d43f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d43f
  clock: 7  # d43f
  nonce: d43f  # d43f
  message: "THE SETTING SHIPPED in PR #2213 (b962b6cc67, dev 6a9720bc8e), 2026-11-16. THIS ITEM STAYS OPEN: its own repro (hypergumbo's self-profile counting the recorded aardvark_dns crate and recorded/sample_project as first-party code) is NOT fixed on dev, because hypergumbo's own .hypergumbo.toml is not in that PR. WHAT SHIPPED: project-tier key test_input_dirs in .hypergumbo.toml (literal repository-relative directories; glob, absolute path, path leaving the repository, missing path, non-directory each exit 2 naming the entry). classify_test_file runs its path rules first, then the declared directories (reason declared_test_input). The declaration is saved in the map (supply_chain_summary.declared_test_inputs, SCHEMA_VERSION 0.21.1) and disclosed on stderr, in the sketch Overview and in the map. WHY A DECLARATION AND NOT A COMPUTED RULE: census of 661 embedded project trees in 44 repositories (notebook stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr3/fosuk_census.md): 'only test code references the tree' finds 6 of 292; 'own manifest that no build includes' finds 37 and wrongly demotes 106 first-party trees. MEASURED: fx (Go) declaring internal/e2e: entry points from it 2 to 0. automerge javascript/ declaring packaging_tests: entry points 42 to 14, dead-code candidates 134 to 78. Repositories with no config: maps identical except schema_version and one pass_version. Stable ids: 0 moved. THE ITEM'S OWN REPRO, measured on a branch that carried the config (not merged): base arm (release 10.0.0 code, clean dev tree) sketch Tests line '1534 test files - cargo test, hypothesis, pytest, unittest' and Entry Points list main of recorded/sample_project/pkg/app.py and recorded/aardvark_dns/crate/src/main.rs; with the config: Overview discloses 22 declared files, no cargo test, neither main; check-self-claims 23 unchanged. OWNER RULINGS 2026-11-16: a repository's own declaration MAY change a verify-claims verdict (disclosed as excluded_flows.declared_test_input_sourced; --include-non-production-sources turns the exclusion off); schema stays 0.21.1 and spec Appendix A was corrected; hypergumbo's own config waits for WI-dahoh-ralop-gilid-gubat-zinul-murob-bufal-dibuk (a released hypergumbo, 10.0.0 included, exits 2 on the unknown key and smart-test slices with the installed release). CLOSE WHEN WI-dahoh lands and the self-profile repro is re-run on dev. NOT CHANGED: the Overview language percentages still include test-only languages; the sketch's Configuration and Additional Files sections can still list files from a declared directory."  # d43f
